#!/bin/bash
# land-budget-in-one-place.sh — the budget stops being a page, folds shut once
# it is set, starts every category at nothing, and honours a zero.
#
# BOTH RAILS. The zero rule is enforced in the planner, not hidden in the view.
# PRECONDITION: land-budget.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-react ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="Zero is an answer"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"No routine before a budget"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-budget.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="c0b11cab9189ad03dada41e70e8ae6dfc60da4e6d0f9bd969a3573cfb5418042"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/beauty src/security
cd ../together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add -A together-city-chat/src/beauty together-city-react/src
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
Zero is an answer

Four corrections to yesterday's budget, all of them the owner's, and the third
is the one with teeth.

ONE PLACE, AND IT IS THE PROFILE. The budget had a page of its own and a
sidebar tab. That was a second location for a single decision — and the
decision belongs directly under the assessment it is spending against, where
you read what your skin needs and then say what you will put behind it without
navigating anywhere. Budget.tsx and its route are deleted and the sidebar is
five items again: Profile, Routine, Market, Makeup, Orders.

IT FOLDS SHUT ONCE IT IS SET. Everything else on that page already did; the
budget was the exception because it was the next thing to do, and it stops
being the next thing to do the moment it is answered. Collapsed, the header
carries the answer — "Face ₹3,000 · Hair ₹2,000 · Body ₹1,500 — ₹6,500/month" —
so it can be read without being opened, with a link straight to the routine.

EVERY DIAL STARTS AT NOTHING. It opened at ₹3,000 / ₹2,000 / ₹1,500, which is
an anchor: people nudge a suggested figure and call the result their choice.
Starting at zero means the number that ends up there is one somebody reached
for. The floor moves with it — the sliders run from ₹0 rather than ₹1,000, the
quick row gains a "None", and emptying the field means zero rather than
"leave it as it was", because being silently overruled is worse than being
taken literally.

AND ZERO MEANS THE CATEGORY IS NOT SHOWN AT ALL. This is the one that had to
reach the planner rather than the page. `planCategory` returns immediately on a
zero budget: no picks, no `leftOut` list, no upgrade suggestions, nothing to
render and nothing to hide. Somebody who leaves Body at nothing is saying they
already have a body wash they like, and the correct response is silence — not
the cheapest lotion we could find, not a tally of what they are missing, not a
nudge to raise it. The routine page then draws no body band, rather than a
heading over an absence.

  IT IS NOT THE SAME AS `null`. Null means no budget has ever been set and gates
  the routine entirely; zero is a decision about one part of a budget that
  exists. Two different silences, and the code says which is which.

  The Create button is disabled while all three are zero rather than saving an
  empty budget and sending somebody to an empty routine to work out why.

budget-is-a-limit.spec.ts gains the case: a zero category plans nothing, lists
nothing, suggests nothing, and does not disturb the two that were funded.

tsc clean both sides. Backend 93 beauty tests plus route-reach green; frontend
60 files, a11y 0 at the ceiling, motion and lint at theirs, vite build clean.

MSG
echo "== committed"

echo
echo "==============================================================="
echo " Landed: $NEEDS"
echo " Budget lives on the profile, folds shut once set, starts at"
echo " nothing, and a zero category is left out entirely."
echo "==============================================================="
